WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.063 --> 00:00:03.457
[MUSIC]

00:00:03.457 --> 00:00:06.130
What am I most excited about for
this year?

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:07.933
That's super easy.

00:00:07.933 --> 00:00:12.846
I'm excited to have everyone back together
and in-person, and we've been waiting for

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:14.101
this for 18 months.

00:00:14.101 --> 00:00:17.488
And today's the first day when
the MBA students are back, and

00:00:17.488 --> 00:00:19.974
it's finally arrived, and it feels great.

00:00:19.974 --> 00:00:22.908
[MUSIC]

00:00:22.908 --> 00:00:25.700
I told the MBA class that they're
arriving at a great time.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.675
And, of course,
part of that is they're arriving and

00:00:28.675 --> 00:00:31.940
we're starting to get toward
the end of the pandemic.

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:35.080
And so the world is opening up,
and Stanford is opening up.

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:37.461
And all of the things that
we've been looking forward to,

00:00:37.461 --> 00:00:38.876
we can start to do again together.

00:00:38.876 --> 00:00:40.249
[MUSIC]

00:00:40.249 --> 00:00:46.133
They're arriving at a time when there's
incredible change going on in the world,

00:00:46.133 --> 00:00:49.507
in technology, in business,
and in society.

00:00:49.507 --> 00:00:54.491
And they're arriving at Stanford at
a time when they can be right in

00:00:54.491 --> 00:00:57.250
the middle of all of that change, and

00:00:57.250 --> 00:01:02.423
thinking about what it is they want to
do with their careers and lives.

00:01:02.423 --> 00:01:03.838
[MUSIC]

00:01:03.838 --> 00:01:09.210
I think there's two big lessons
from the experience going

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:14.811
through the pandemic and
teaching and interacting online.

00:01:14.811 --> 00:01:18.741
One was a positive, which was,
it was sort of revelation what

00:01:18.741 --> 00:01:22.142
you could do virtually in
terms of getting work done,

00:01:22.142 --> 00:01:26.615
and having classes, and keeping
even a place like Stanford running.

00:01:26.615 --> 00:01:31.595
The other was, there's just a set of
things that happen at a business school,

00:01:31.595 --> 00:01:36.240
at a university,
that you can't replicate with technology.

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:39.843
And if you think back before the pandemic,
in the case of MBA programs,

00:01:39.843 --> 00:01:44.005
people were actually questioning, is
there value in a residential MBA program?

00:01:44.005 --> 00:01:49.135
And if the pandemic just definitively
answered that question in a positive way?

00:01:49.135 --> 00:01:54.018
Yes, there's just something about being
with a group of people, students, and

00:01:54.018 --> 00:01:57.861
the faculty, and with the mix of
people that comes onto campus.

00:01:57.861 --> 00:02:02.054
And just being in it that we still
can't do with technology, and

00:02:02.054 --> 00:02:05.095
we can do it here on a place
like the GSB campus.

00:02:05.095 --> 00:02:12.047
[MUSIC]

00:02:12.047 --> 00:02:14.520
My go-to drink or
order at Coupa, it's so boring.

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:16.211
It's just a small black coffee.

00:02:16.211 --> 00:02:19.877
[MUSIC]

00:02:19.877 --> 00:02:23.380
I've been running a lot
up in the foothills.

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:28.700
And every time I get out in the California
foothills, it just reminds me

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:34.922
why I moved out to California in the first
place and why I've never left this place.

00:02:34.922 --> 00:02:43.003
[MUSIC]

